X:1
T:Tôn Garol (version 2)
T:Mwynder Mai
R:carol
B:The Welsh Harper (1848)
S:Sent by Steve Jeans, from the Plygain books and Canu Haf
N:In three parts, with the tune in the middle part. The words under the notes are a Plygain carol for Christmas by Rhys Prichard (c.1575–1644). After them is a spring carol on the same tune, Mwynder Mai, by T. Gwynn Jones (1871–1949), which Steve learnt from Arfon Gwilym.
N:In Mwynder Mai, the c/d/ in bar 15 of the tune is one c.
M:3/4
L:1/4
